.TH SKEIN 1 "2026-07-26" "skein 0.3.48" "Skein Manual"
.SH NAME
skein \- context-first, model-agnostic coding agent with an auditable terminal workspace
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B skein
[options] [command] [prompt...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Usage: skein [options] [command] [prompt...]

A context-first, model-agnostic coding agent with an auditable workspace.

Arguments:
  prompt                     instruction for the agent

Options:
  -V, --version              output the version number
  -p, --print                run once and print the result
  -a, --ask                  retrieval and inspection mode; mutation tools are
                             denied
  --plan                     read-only planning mode; propose changes without
                             mutating the workspace
  -q, --quiet                print only the final response in text mode
  --output-format <format>   text, json, or stream-json (choices: "text",
                             "json", "stream-json", default: "text")
  --compact                  reduce progress output in print mode
  --yes                      approve all non-denied tool requests for this run
  --auto-edit                approve read/write requests and ask before
                             shell/Git/network
  --trust-project-config     allow executable and security-sensitive settings
                             from project config
  --queue <prompt>           run an additional prompt after the first one
                             (default: [])
  -w, --workspace <path>     primary workspace root (default:
                             "/Users/jiming/codeagentcli")
  --add-workspace <path>     additional workspace root (default: [])
  --config <path>            explicit config file
  --connection <name>        named model connection
  --provider <provider>      model provider
  --model <model>            model identifier
  --base-url <url>           OpenAI-compatible or provider base URL
  --max-turns <n>            maximum agent turns
  --epoch-token-budget <n>   maximum tokens before an internal context handoff
  --token-budget <n>         maximum lifetime tokens across the resumed session
  --resume [session]         resume a session by id or prefix
  -c, --continue             resume the latest session
  --no-color                 disable color output
  --no-checkpoint            disable pre-mutation checkpoints for this run
  -h, --help                 display help for command

Getting started:
  init [options]             Create a project-local config (preserving an
                             existing .mosaic namespace)
  config                     Inspect the resolved configuration
  status [options]           Show model, context, workspace, and index status
  doctor [options]           Diagnose prerequisites and safe fallbacks
  update [options]           Update to the latest published release
  migrate [options]          Inspect or migrate legacy .mosaic state into .skein
  completion <shell>         Generate completion for bash, zsh, or fish
  feedback                   Show where to report issues, with a content-free
                             environment summary

Context & retrieval:
  index [options]            Index the configured workspace
  search [options] <query>   Search indexed code and print grounded file spans
  context [options] <query>  Pack task-oriented context under a token budget

Sessions & recovery:
  session                    Manage local, resumable sessions
  jobs                       Manage optional durable background jobs
  checkpoint                 Inspect and restore pre-mutation snapshots

Agents & extensions:
  tools [options]            List active built-in agent tools and permission
                             categories
  skills                     Discover task-specific Agent Skills
  agents                     Inspect specialized agent profiles
  workflow                   Inspect typed coding workflows
  memory                     Manage durable local memory
  mcp                        Inspect configured MCP servers
  rules [options]            List user and workspace rules loaded into the agent

Examples:
  $ skein                                   start the interactive workspace
  $ skein "fix the failing webhook test"    run one instruction interactively
  $ skein -p "explain src/agent/runner.ts"  run once and print the result
  $ git diff | skein -p "review this diff"  include piped stdin in the prompt
  $ skein search "token budget"             search the local code index
  $ skein --continue                        resume the latest session

Learn more:
  Website  https://lixiang12345.github.io/skein/
  Docs     https://github.com/lixiang12345/skein/blob/main/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
  Issues   https://github.com/lixiang12345/skein/issues
.fi
.SH COMMANDS
.SS skein init
.nf
Usage: skein init [options]

Create a project-local config (preserving an existing .mosaic namespace)

Options:
  -w, --workspace <path>  workspace root
  --provider <provider>   openai, anthropic, gemini, or compatible (default:
                          "openai")
  --model <model>         model identifier
  --base-url <url>        provider base URL
  --api-key <key>         store a provider key in project config (prefer env
                          vars)
  --index                 build the index after writing config
  --yes                   use defaults without prompting
  -h, --help              display help for command
.fi
.SS skein config
.nf
Usage: skein config [options] [command]

Inspect the resolved configuration

Options:
  -h, --help      display help for command

Commands:
  show [options]  Show effective configuration with secrets redacted
  path [options]  Show the project config path
  help [command]  display help for command
.fi
.SS skein status
.nf
Usage: skein status [options]

Show model, context, workspace, and index status

